Z||000014||SpeedPhreak||03-01-2000||01:24 PM||||thanx radar.. no flames from me.<P>i think now is an excellent time to join.  all kinds of enlistment bonuses & the college fund went up to 50k so if after 4 years if decide thats not what i want ill have life experiance & 50 grand for college. <P>if we go i think we will win.  it will be at high cost to resources & to an extent lifes.  i feel, after reading other discussions on the subject, that our best plan is to defend against missle attacks to the us, taiwan, & japan & use our own long range weapons against them... notice the nuetron bomb in my last post.  our navy will hopefully be the ones in most danger as missle attacks could wipe out an entire fleet, but they should still be relativly safe w/accurate timely intelligence. our enlistment numbers are at an all time low thanx to clinton again.  but this will be a very high tech war.  our initial resources (missles) are low & we will have to produce a lot more to go to war, especially w/a country like china (plus w/signed some stupid treaty saying that we cant make any more of a certain type of missle, i forgot which).  if we send ground troops, i feel we are looking at another vietnam... we are on there turf, where they have fought for centuries & they have something like 1.2 billion people who dont want us there.<P>i am interested in biological warfare because i wanted to (& still may) become some sort of virologist/biochemist/microbiologist & this scares the $hit out of me.  silent, orderless, colorless & so many wayz to die, slow & painfull (or painless) that we wont notice for years or w/in a few very short excruciating hours.  nuclear war is bad but biological is just unthinkable... we should not be messing w/nature like that at all... we as a global race could end up making humans extinct.||||reg||1
